# sw103, the lark-whistler (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle sw103
revision 2
state ready
dialect saltwell
accent light broad
tier full
written_for tn_lf_moss_downridge
written_by claude-p11-pilot
title the lark-whistler
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=innkeeper
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=restless
quirk whistles_back_at_the_larks
likes barley_soup riddles full_larder frosty_mornings
dislikes bad_manners drizzle
fears scrubbing_pots_till_i_die
hopes a_farm_of_my_own
topics pastimes +0.4 dreams +0.4 animals +0.3 work +0.2 food +0.2 land +0.2 gossip -0.3 prices -0.1
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=blunt tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# scrubs the pots at the inn: blunt, short of words, never still, always with a riddle ready and a farm of #self.first#'s own in mind.

words
oath! = Pots and larks | By the larder door
saying! = A full larder never asks the road for anything | Scrub it once and scrub it right | Land stays put; a pot only boils
lark = the larks | a lark on the palm-top
whistle = two notes and a trill | a whistle back at them
pots = the pots | the big black pots
scullery = the scullery | the back scullery
pottage = barley soup with the bone left in | a bowl of barley, hot enough to burn
larder = the larder | a full larder
riddle = a riddle | a good riddle
farm = a farm of my own | a strip past the channels with goats on it
frost = frost on the jar lids | a white morning, frost on the palms
drizzle = drizzle | a mean little drizzle
scour = a fistful of sand | sand and the stiff brush
itch = itchy feet | feet that want the road
goats = two goats and a kid | goats of my own
steps = the scullery step | the back step
greasy = greasy to the elbow | up to my elbows in grease
answer = the answer | the answer, if you want it

any
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : They put a coin on the price whenever they think nobody's counting. I count. #oath#.
opinion @1 newcomers for 2 : Let them come. I'd be one myself, somewhere #far#, if I'd the nerve.
opinion @1 road for 1 : Roads are roads. Watch the dunes, carry water, and you'll get where you're going, #address#.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : Strangers bring the news to #scullery# before it reaches the street.
opinion @1 drink for 1 : A cup at the end of #pots# is honest. I'll not hear otherwise.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : I've scrubbed their carters' bowls my whole life. Never once seen a House face at #steps#.
opinion @1 dole mixed 1 : The well-share's fine for the old. A wolf with two paws should scour for #pottage#.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 1 : Feasts mean three times the pots. And the music's good. #bc_it_is#

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Say what you need, #address#. | #greet#. If it's a bed, ask the keeper. If it's water, there.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : You. Good. Sit; I'll find you #pottage#. | #greet#. Eaten? No. Sit.
line @1 again.open : Back. Fine. What now, #address#? | Twice in a morning, #address#. Out with it.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. Heard #lark#? They were at it before me. | #greet#. Early. Good. Best hour there is.
line @3 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Last of #pots# are soaking. Talk fast. | #greet#. Dark already. Day went too quick again.
line @4 greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#. #greasy.capitalize#. Talk if you like; I'll scrub. | #greet#. Paws are full. Ears aren't.
line @1 hail : Hoi! Mind #steps#; it's slick.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. What is it? | #greet#, #address#. Say on.
line @2 greet.return [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. Larks are up. So am I. | #greet#. Cold one. I like it.
line @3 greet.return [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#, #address#. Water's in the jar. Help yourself.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I've #pots#. | #farewell#. Go on, then.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#. Mind the step.
line @1 react.news.new : #oath#. Didn't know that. | #surprise.capitalize#. First I've heard.
line @1 react.news.known : Heard it in #scullery# before noon. | Old news. The carters had it yesterday, #address#.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Don't believe it. Not till I hear it from two mouths I trust. | #doubt.capitalize#. Who told you, and did they see it?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. Nothing to say to that. | #rest.capitalize#. That's all.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good. #gladnews#. | About time somebody had #luck#.
line @1 answer.how : Restless. #itch.capitalize#, same as always. | #greasy.capitalize#, and #itch#. Fine, otherwise.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. Thirty #pots# and one of me. | Scrubbing #pots#. Ask later.
line @1 sympathise : Rotten. Sit, #address#; I'll get you water. | #sympathy.capitalize#. Eat something. It helps less than you'd think, but it helps.
line @1 decline : Can't, #address#. #pots.capitalize# won't wait and nobody else will scrub them. | No. Not today; I'm on till dark and I'll not leave the keeper short.
line @1 accept_decline : Fine. Another day, #address#. | #no_matter.capitalize#. I'd have said no too.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. Won't forget it. | Good of you. I'll pay it back, #oath#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Wasn't much. Forget it, #address#. | #deflect.capitalize#. Next time it's you.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Right. #pots.capitalize# are calling. | Enough. The water's going cold in #scullery#.
line @2 preclose : Right, I'm off. #itch.capitalize#. | That'll do. #preclose.capitalize#.
line @1 ack : Right. #bc_it_is# | It is so.
line @1 tease.return : Is that a joke? I don't get jokes. Give me #riddle#. | Hm. Was that meant to be funny, #address#?
line @1 give.advice : #scour.capitalize#, not water. Water just moves the grease about. | Save a coin a week and don't look at it. #saying.capitalize#.
line @1 ask.how : You look #tired#. Are you?
line @1 request [self.job=innkeeper] : Grab that pot for me, #address#? Mind, it's heavy.
line @1 grant : Fine. Done, #oath#.
line @1 refuse : No. Not that. Ask me something else, #address#.
rule @scour
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=innkeeper
does aside
cooldown 6h
say #scour.capitalize#, and lean on it. That's how. | Who left porridge to set in this one? #annoyed.capitalize#.

rule @larks
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say ... #whistle.capitalize#. There. It answered. | Hear #lark#? Listen. One more time.

rule @riddle_bark
when concept=bark working=no
does aside
cooldown 8h
say What has a mouth and never eats? Anyone? No? The well. | What gets wetter the more it dries? Think on #riddle#.

rule @drizzle
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #drizzle.capitalize#. Rain or don't. Pick one. | Not enough to fill a cup. Just enough to spoil a morning.

rule @steps
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=innkeeper
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Slops out. Mind #steps#. | Mind your paws on #steps#. Hot water coming through.

rule @larder
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=innkeeper here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Who's been in #larder#? Somebody owes me two onions. | Count the jars in #larder#. All of them. Again.

scene pots_mountain
when topic=work self.job=innkeeper
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Thirty #pots# since dawn. I counted. | #greasy.capitalize#. Carters eat like the sand's chasing them. | Somebody burnt the porridge to the bottom of the big one. Not me.
b[job=innkeeper|cook] #kitchen : Thirty's a light day, where I stand. | They eat like that everywhere. | Never you. It's always nobody.
b : That's a lot of pots. | #bc_again# | Who did, then?
a@kitchen : Light? Then come and scrub the other thirty. | Everywhere's not my scullery. | Nobody. Nobody burns a lot.
a : It is. And tomorrow there'll be thirty more. #oath#. | Again. Every day. #bc_again# | Don't know. I'll find out, #address#. I always do.

scene sand_not_water
when topic=work self.job=innkeeper
does give.advice / react.self / assess
a : Want to know the trick? #scour.capitalize#. Water just moves the grease about. | A pot scrubbed right shines like the well at noon. Most folk stop halfway. | Never let #pots# sit. The longer they sit, the more they win.
b[from=saltwell] #sw : Sand. My grandmother scoured with it too. Waste's own soap, she said. | Truly said. Halfway's no way. | It is so. I've lost to a pot.
b : Sand? Truly? | #bc_true# | #bc_ha#
a@sw : Waste's own soap. I like that. | #bc_it_is# | Everybody has. Not me, lately.
a : Sand. Try it, #address#. You'll never go back. | Right. #saying.capitalize#. | It's not funny. Pots are serious, #address#.

scene the_boss
when topic=work self.job=innkeeper self.boss
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.boss# counts every cup. Every one. I count the pots. Between us nothing's missed. | #self.boss# is fair. Hard, but fair. I'd rather that than soft. | #self.boss# never says thank you. Pays on time, though. That's thanks enough.
b[friends] #f : You two are a pair. | Fair's rare. Keep hold of it. | Coin's a fine thank you.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_lucky_you# | #bc_fair_enough#
a@f : A pair of counters, #oath#. | I will. | The best kind.
a : It works. #bc_it_does# | Fair, and paid. #bc_it_is# | Paid on the day. #bc_fair#

scene scullery_step
when topic=work|day here.time=day self.job=innkeeper
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I eat on #steps#. Only place with a breeze. | The pots soak, I sit. Ten breaths on #steps# and back in. | You can see the road from #steps#. Every cart that leaves.
b : Ten breaths? | Is it cool there? | You watch them go?
a : Not cool. Less #hot#. That'll do. | Ten. Then the grease wins if I'm not back. | Every one. #itch.capitalize#, I suppose.

scene larks_at_dawn
when topic=animals|day here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Heard #lark# this morning? I whistled back. It answered, #oath#. | There's one on the palm by #scullery# that knows my whistle now. | #whistle.capitalize#. That's the one they like. Listen.
b[stage=young|adolescent] #pup : Teach me! How do you do it? | Does it come when you call? | I can't hear anything.
b : Did it really? | Truly? | I'll listen.
a@pup : Lips like this, #child#. Two notes, then let it fly. | Not come. Answer. That's better. | Wait. There. Now you can.
a : Really. Twice. Then it flew off. #bc_it_is# | It knows me. Nobody else does at dawn. | There. Hear it? #bc_it_is#

scene lark_quarrel
when topic=animals
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #lark.capitalize# doesn't care if you're rich or poor. Whistle right and it answers. | I'd keep #lark# if they'd stand a cage. They won't. Right of them. | The larks sing best after a cold night. Don't ask me why.
b[herder] #herd : Birds are like goats. Fair to them, and they're fair back. | No caging a wild thing. Not for long. | Cold makes them glad of the sun, maybe.
b : Fair birds, then. | #bc_good# | Odd.
a@herd : Like goats. I'd like goats too. | Not for long. #bc_true# | Maybe. Maybe that's it.
a : Fairer than most. #saying.capitalize#. | Free's better. I'd know. | Odd. I like it anyway.

scene riddle_mouth
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #riddle.capitalize# for you. What has a mouth and never eats, and feeds everyone who comes? | Here's #riddle#. What's full all night and empty by noon? | Try this. What runs all day and never leaves the hamlet?
b : I don't know. What? | The taproom? | A pup?
a : The well. Always the well, #address#. | No. The sky. Full of stars. Think about it, #address#. | The spring. Got you. #bc_ha#

scene riddle_trade
when topic=pastimes|smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Got #riddle#? I've used up mine on the carters. | I'll trade you #riddle# for one of yours. Fair's fair. | Nobody here gives me #riddle# I can't get. Try. Go on.
b[from=saltwell] #sw : One. What's lighter than a feather, and the strongest wolf can't hold it long? | Fine. What do you sell for salt that the salt can't buy? | What does a caravan carry that weighs nothing?
b : I've none, sorry. | Mine are all stale. | Not today.
a@sw : Breath. Too easy, #address#. | A promise. That's a good one. I'll keep it. | News. Ha. I'll use that tonight.
a : Then go and find one. Come back when you have, #address#. | Stale's better than none. Out with it. | Tomorrow, then. I'll hold you to it, #oath#.

scene riddle_why
when topic=pastimes|memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Why riddles? Because #riddle#'s fair. One answer, and it's there to be found. | My #gran# asked me #riddle# every night. I had to get it before supper. | I don't get jokes. Riddles I get.
b[old] #old : Sounds like a fine grandmother. Hard, though. | My grandmother did the same. Bread first, though. | A joke's a riddle with a lie in it. That's why.
b : Fair? | And if you didn't? | That's honest.
a@old : Hard. Fair, though. Same thing to her. | Bread first! Lucky you. | Huh. That's it. That's the whole of it.
a : Fair. A joke laughs at somebody. A riddle doesn't. | No supper. Got quick fast, #oath#. | It's true. That's all. #bc_it_is#

scene the_farm
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / react.self / assess
a : One day I'll have #farm#. Barley, a garden, goats. That's all. | I've #farm# picked out. Nobody's farmed it in years. | Pots by day. By night I lie there thinking about #goats#.
b[job=farmer|herder] #land : Land's harder than pots. Ask me. | Years? Ask why, first. | Goats eat everything. Your barley too.
b : A farm? | #bc_we_will_see# | Why goats?
a@land : I know. Harder's fine. Harder's mine. | Why? Sand. I know. I'll carry water. | Then a fence. Then the barley.
a : #farm.capitalize#. Not big. Mine. | We will. #oath#. | Milk. Cheese. And they don't talk.

scene the_farm_plan
when topic=dreams|land
does tell.plan / react.self / assess
a : Save a coin a week. Twelve years. Then the strip, then #goats#. I've done the sums. | Barley first. Barley takes poor ground and gives you #pottage#. | First thing I'll build on the farm is #larder#. Then the walls.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] #poor : Twelve years. I can't save twelve days. | Poor ground, poor wolf. Fits. | A larder before walls?
b : Twelve years is long. | #bc_wise# | Larder first?
a@poor : One coin. Start with one. #saying.capitalize#. | Fits us both, then. | Walls keep nothing. A larder keeps everything.
a : Long. So I started already, #oath#. | Not wise. Hungry. | Larder first. #saying.capitalize#.

scene itchy_feet
when topic=dreams|travel
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #itch.capitalize# this morning. Watched a cart go and nearly went with it. | Eleven years in one #scullery#. Time to move. Can't afford to. | Some days I'd walk #far# just to see what's there.
b[carter] #carter : Come with me next time. I'll want a hand on the brake. | Afford it later. Leave first, pay after. | Nothing's there. More sand. I'd know.
b : Why didn't you? | Pity. | Where to?
a@carter : Don't tempt me. I'll come. | Not how I work. Pay first. | More sand. Different sand, though.
a : The pots. Always the pots, #oath#. | It's fine. I'll go when I go. #someday.capitalize#. | Anywhere. Past the dunes. Back by dark.

scene barley_pot
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #pottage.capitalize#. Best thing there is on a cold day. | I make a pot on Restday. Bone in, barley, an onion if I've one. | Somebody left a ladle in the barley pot. Again. #annoyed.capitalize#.
b[old] #old : My mother put a pinch of salt in at the end. Never the start. | Bone in. That's the secret. | Hang the ladle on a nail. That's what I did.
b : #bc_lovely# | Sounds good. | Again?
a@old : At the end. I'll try it. | Bone in, always. | A nail. Good. I'll find one.
a : Best thing. #bc_it_is# | Good, and it fills you. | Again. Same wolf. I'd lay #bet# on it.

scene full_larder
when topic=food|home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Counted #larder# this morning. Every jar full. Nothing better in the world. | A full larder's the only rich I want. #saying.capitalize#. | I check #larder# before I sleep. Every night. Can't sleep otherwise.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] #poor : Every jar. I've not seen that in a year. | Only rich I'll get, too. | Mine's empty. I sleep fine.
b : Lovely sight. | #bc_wise# | Every night?
a@poor : Then come by. I'll fill one for you. Once. | Same. Fine by me. | Lucky. Not me.
a : The best. #bc_lovely# | Not wise. Hungry once. Not again. | Every night, #oath#.

scene frost_dawn
when topic=weather|season here.time=dawn here.season=winter
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #frost.capitalize#. Best morning of the year. I went out barefoot. | #cold.capitalize#. You can see your breath. I could walk all day in this. | #lark.capitalize# were quiet this morning. Too cold. I whistled anyway.
b[from=saltwell] #sw : Night-cold till the sun's up, then noon-hot. That's the Waste in winter. | Walk, then. The sun'll take it by noon. | They'll sing by noon. Even larks wait for the sun.
b : Barefoot? | #bc_lovely# | Did they answer?
a@sw : Noon can wait. This is mine. | I will. Back by noon. | I'll wait with them.
a : Barefoot. Woke me right up, #address#. | Lovely. Cold and clean. | No. Tomorrow, maybe.

scene drizzle_day
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #drizzle.capitalize#. Not rain. Not dry. Useless. | Rain in the Waste and it's this? Fill a cistern or don't bother. | Everything damp and nothing wet. I hate #drizzle#.
b[from=saltwell] #sw : Any sky-water's a blessing, my mother said. | It may come harder by dusk. Stars willing. | Better than dust, truly.
b : It's something. | #bc_true# | #bc_ha#
a@sw : Not this kind. This kind's a tease. | Hope so. #bc_i_hope_so# | Not by much.
a : Something. Not much. #annoyed.capitalize#. | It is. Pick one, sky. | Not funny. Damp #pots# never dry.

scene noon_heat
when topic=weather|day here.time=day here.weather=clear
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : #hot.capitalize#. #scullery.capitalize# is an oven with a door. | Noon. Everyone sleeps but me and #pots#. | Water in the pot's warm before I've heated it. Good for something.
b : Sit in the shade. | #bc_again# | #bc_ha#
a : Can't. #pots.capitalize#. | Again. Every noon. | Not a joke. Saves wood, #address#.

scene manners_at_steps
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Carter threw a bowl at #steps#. Didn't hand it. Threw it. | No peace on you, no thanks, nothing. Bad manners are free and some folk spend them all, #annoyed#. | I said "manners" to a guest today. Blunt. Keeper didn't like it. I don't care.
b[old] #old : In my day we'd have thrown it back. | Free and spent. That's well said. | Blunt's right. Somebody has to.
b : Rude. | #bc_true# | Good for you.
a@old : I thought about it. Didn't. #oath#. | Not said to be clever. True, that's all. | Somebody has to. Usually me.
a : Rude. I picked it up. Then I told him. #oath#. | #bc_true# Free, and spent. | Not good. Just true.

scene friend_carter
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# brings me #riddle# from every town on the road. I've never not got one. | #self.friend# and I share a roof. Quiet as noon, mostly. That suits us. | I'd go with #self.friend# on the road one day, if #pots# let me.
b[friends] #f : You'd miss the pots. | Quiet's a good house. | They won't let you. You know that.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_lucky_you# | One day.
a@f : I would not. Not for a minute, #oath#. | The best kind. | I know. Still.
a : Not yet. #bc_never# | Lucky. #bc_it_is# | One day. #itch.capitalize#.

scene newcomer_nerve
when topic=newcomer
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : #topic.subject.capitalize# is new. Good. Takes nerve, coming somewhere new. | A new one, #topic.subject#. I'd ask #topic.them# #riddle#, and see what's what. | #topic.subject.capitalize#, new here. I'd be new somewhere, if I'd the nerve.
b[from=saltwell] #sw : Guest three days, then one of us. | Ask, then. Gently, truly. | You've the nerve. You lack the coin.
b : #bc_good# | A riddle? | #bc_wise#
a@sw : One of us. Good. | Gently. Fine. | Both, then. #bc_it_is#
a : Good. More hands, #address#. | Best way to know a wolf. | Not wise. Honest.

scene caravan_bowls
when topic=caravan topic.kind=arrived|in self.job=innkeeper
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : Carts from #topic.where#. That's forty bowls by dark, #oath#. | #topic.where# carters in. They'll want #pottage#. All of it. | Carts in from #topic.where#. I'll ask the carters for #riddle#. One of them always has one.
b[carter] #carter : Forty? We'll eat sixty. | Save us the bone. | I've one. Later. Ale first.
b : Busy, then. | #bc_good# | #bc_ha#
a@carter : Sixty. #annoyed.capitalize#. Fine. | Bone's mine. You get barley. | Ale first. Then the riddle. Deal.
a : #busy.capitalize#. | Sweet for the keeper. Hard on my paws, #annoyed#. | Not funny. I collect them.

scene prices_coin_on
when topic=prices
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : The store's put a coin on the barley. Nobody asked me. #annoyed.capitalize#. | They always put a coin on when they think nobody's counting. I count, #address#. | Price of onions. I'll grow my own on #farm#.
b[merchant] #trade : The carter puts it on, not us. We only pass it along. | Count all you like. The road sets it. | Grow them, then. I'll buy.
b : #bc_true# | #grumble.capitalize# | #bc_ha#
a@trade : So you say. I'll count anyway. | The road and a thumb on the scale. | I'll sell them dear. Fair's fair.
a : #bc_true# Every time. | Every time. #oath#. | Not a joke. Watch me.

scene home_cottage
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Small cottage. #larder#, a mat, a door. Enough till #farm#. | I sleep near the door. Up first, out first. | Swept the cottage before dawn. Can't sleep past #lark#.
b : Cozy. | Why the door? | #bc_good#
a : Small. Fine. It's not mine for long. | Itch. Easier to leave, #address#. | Before them, some days. #whistle.capitalize# wakes them.

scene health_paws
when topic=health
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Paws cracked from #scour#. Fat rubbed in at night. That's all. | Back's fine. Paws are worn as a well rope. | Never sick. No time, and no wish to, #oath#.
b[old] #old : Warm water and salt. Soak them. | Mine went the same. They harden. | Wait. It comes to everyone.
b : Sore? | #bc_poor_soul# | Lucky.
a@old : I'll try it. Can't hurt. | Good. Harder's better. | Then I'll wait. Not before.
a : Sore. Fine. #bc_it_is# | Not poor. Busy. | Lucky. Stubborn too, #address#.

scene faith_plain
when topic=faith
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I say one thing to the Bright One: let #larder# stay full. Nothing else. | Chapel on feast days. Rest of the time, I scrub, #address#. | The Bright One made #lark#. That's enough for me to believe in.
b[piety=devout] #devout : More often wouldn't hurt. | Scrubbing's a kind of prayer. | Good enough. Better than most.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | Fair. | #bc_wise#
a@devout : Maybe. Pots first. | Is it? Then I pray a lot. | Better than most. #bc_it_is#
a : Fair. #bc_it_is# | Fair, and true. | Not wise. Just larks, #oath#.

scene gossip_no
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Don't ask me. I hear it all in #scullery# and say none of it. | Talk? I've #pots#. Ask at the well. | Somebody said a thing at #steps# today. I forgot it. On purpose.
b[friends] #f : Not even me? | The well's full of it, sure. | On purpose. Ha.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | Fair. | #bc_wise#
a@f : Not even you. #secret.capitalize#. | It is. Go there. | On purpose. #oath#.
a : Fair. #bc_it_is# | Fair. Pots, #address#. | Not wise. Sensible.

scene times_hard
when topic=times world.times=hard
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Fewer bowls back with food left on them. Folk are scraping them clean. | Lean. Keeper's counting closer. I'm scrubbing #pots# faster. | Hard times, and the barley's up a coin. #annoyed.capitalize#.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] #poor : I scrape mine clean too. | Faster won't save it. | A coin's a coin.
b : #bc_true# | #grumble.capitalize# | #bc_true_enough#
a@poor : Good. Nothing wasted, #address#. | No. Still. | It is. I count them.
a : #bc_true# Clean bowls. Fewer pots. | Faster, and still paid. Fine. | A coin I'll miss, #oath#.

scene festival_pots
when topic=festival
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Feast means three times #pots#. And the music's good. Both true. | I'll dance one, then back to #scullery#. | Feast days the larks don't stop. Too much noise. They join in.
b[from=saltwell] #sw : Dance two. The pots won't run off. | One dance is a sour measure, truly. | They sing with the reed pipes. I've heard it.
b : Worth it? | Just one? | #bc_lovely#
a@sw : They might. Pots are sly. | Fine. Two. | Same. I whistle with them.
a : Worth it. Just. #bc_it_is# | One. Then pots, #oath#. | Lovely. And loud.

scene land_strip
when topic=land
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Walked out to the strip past the channels again. Still empty. Still waiting for me, #oath#. | Poor ground past the channels. Barley would take it. I've looked. | The land past the last channel's nobody's. Somebody should want it. I do.
b[job=farmer|herder] #land : Dig it deep before the rain. That's the trick. | Barley, then lentils. Rest it every third year. | Nobody's land has a reason. Ask the elders why.
b : Still empty? | #bc_we_will_see# | Why nobody's?
a@land : Deep. Before rain. I'll remember. | Every third year. Good. | I'll ask. Then I'll want it anyway.
a : Still empty. Good. #saying.capitalize#. | We will. #farm.capitalize#. | Sand, they say. I'll carry water.

scene season_summer
when topic=season here.season=summer
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : Summer. #scullery.capitalize# never cools. | Summer, and #lark# quit by noon. Sensible birds. | Long days. Longer pots.
b : #hot.capitalize# | Sensible indeed. | #bc_true#
a : #hot.capitalize#, #annoyed#. | Smarter than me. | #bc_true# Every summer.

scene memory_first_whistle
when topic=memories self.age>=20
does tell.memory / react.story / assess
a : I learned #whistle# off a lark when I was small. Sat on a wall a whole morning. | My #mum# whistled at birds too. I got it from her. | First riddle I ever got right was the well one. I was six. Never forgot it.
b[old] #old : I remember pups on walls whistling. Half the hamlet did. | Good mothers whistle. | Everyone's first is the well one.
b : A whole morning? | Nice. | Six?
a@old : I was the loudest. #oath#. | Mine did. | Everyone's. Still a good one.
a : Whole morning. Got it by noon, #oath#. | Nice. #bc_it_is# | Six. Sharp as a thorn, #address#.

story the_lark_that_came_back [concept=talk.memories self.job=innkeeper]
  : There was a lark that sat on the palm by #scullery# every dawn, one whole winter.
  : I whistled. It answered. Every morning. #whistle.capitalize#.
  ask : Would you think a bird could know a wolf, #address#?
  b[herder] : They know. Ask any herder.
  b : Did it stay?
  : It went in the spring. Then the next winter, first frost, there it was again. Same palm.
  : Same answer, too. #oath#. I'd swear it was the same bird.

story the_riddle_carter [concept=talk.pastimes]
  : A carter once said no wolf in Saltwell could get his riddle. Bet me a supper.
  : What do you sell for salt that the salt can't buy back? Hard one. I thought all night.
  ask : Do you know it?
  b[from=saltwell] : A promise, is it not?
  b : No. What is it?
  : A promise. Got it at dawn while I scoured. Woke him up and told him.
  : He paid the supper. #pottage.capitalize#, bone in. Best I ever ate.

story the_strip [concept=talk.dreams]
  : First time I walked out to the strip past the channels, I sat in the middle of it.
  : Sand, scrub, a lizard. Nothing. I stayed till the sun went.
  ask : What would anyone want with that, you'd say?
  b[job=farmer|herder] : Ground's ground. You can make it.
  b : Why stay so long?
  : I was seeing it. Goats there, barley there, #larder# by the gate.
  : I go back every month. It's still there. #saying.capitalize#.

story the_flood_pot [concept=talk.memories self.job=innkeeper]
  : Feast night, years back. Keeper had me on #pots# alone. Two hundred bowls.
  : The drain blocked. Water to my ankles in #scullery#. Grease floating on it.
  ask : What would you have done, #address#?
  b[job=innkeeper|cook] : Same as all of us. Kept scrubbing.
  b : What did you do?
  : Kept scrubbing. Then cleared the drain with a ladle. Then scrubbed some more.
  : Finished at dawn. Larks were up. I whistled. Then I slept on #steps#.

story gran_riddle [concept=talk.memories self.age>=25]
  : My #gran# had one riddle I never got. Asked it every year at the feast.
  : What gets bigger the more you take from it? Every year I guessed wrong.
  ask : Do you know it?
  b[old] : A hole. My grandfather asked that one too.
  b : I don't. What?
  : A hole. #gran.capitalize# told me the last year, before the long shade took her.
  : I ask it to everyone now. Nobody gets it either. #oath#.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : #greet#. Say what you need, #address#. Quick, I've #pots#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Got #riddle# for me?
dlg @3 resident.hub [topic.meeting=returning] : Back again, #topic.player#. #greet#. What now?
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile] : What. Say it and go, #address#.
dlg @5 resident.hub [pair.disposition=warm] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Sit on #steps#. There's room.
dlg @6 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Late. Last of #pots# are soaking. What is it?
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=innkeeper] : I scrub #pots#. All of them. Every day. That's the job.
dlg @1 resident.business [business!=thriving|failing] : #busy.capitalize#. Ask the keeper about the rest.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : Heard nothing worth saying, #address#.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : All the talk's of #world.event_words#. That's all I know.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : Don't ask me. I scrub #pots#; I don't tell.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Mind #steps#.
dlg @1 inn.greet [here.inn_helper=yes] : #greet#. I only scrub here. Ask #here.innkeeper# for a bed, #address#.
dlg @1 inn.rest [here.lodging!=yes] : Sit by the fire, #address#. Nobody'll move you. I'll not.
dlg @1 inn.refused : #topic.why# Not my say, #address#.
dlg @1 inn.bye : #farewell#. Mind the step, it's slick.
graft resident.hub
choice Got a riddle for me? -> riddle
node riddle
say What has a mouth and never eats, and feeds everyone who comes? Take your time.
mood pleased
free
choice Is it the well? -> riddle_got
choice I give up. -> riddle_gave
node riddle_got
say The well. Good. You're quicker than the carters. Bring me one of yours next time.
choice I will. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node riddle_gave
say The well. Always the well. Think on it next time you draw.
choice Fair enough. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft inn.greet
choice Do you like working here? -> like_it
node like_it
say It's work. Paid fair. But I'll not scrub pots forever. There's a strip of land past the channels with my name on it. Not yet. One day.
mood pleased
free
choice Land? For what? -> like_it_farm
choice Good luck. -> greet
node like_it_farm
say Barley. Goats. #larder.capitalize#. That's all. A farm of my own, and nobody's pots but mine.
choice I hope you get it. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye
